{% extends "layouts/app.njk" %}

{#
  What a judge gets for a referral api will not show them — withdrawn, closed, another judge's, or never there.

  Its own page rather than the shared "Page not found" because those two say different things: a judge who
  followed a link from a pool that has since moved on has not mistyped a URL, and the way out is the list rather
  than the browser's back button. The body must stay true of all four causes at once — api answers them
  identically on purpose (decision 10) — so it never says which one happened or who holds the referral.
#}
{% block content %}
<div class="govuk-grid-row">
  <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
    <h1 class="govuk-heading-xl">{{ heading }}</h1>
    <p class="govuk-body">{{ body }}</p>
    <p class="govuk-body">
      <a class="govuk-link" href="{{ poolPath }}">{{ backToPool }}</a>
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
{% endblock %}
